  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the local planning authority hereby certify that on 31st March 2005 the proposed erection of a ground floor rear extension measuring 3.6m deep, 5.1m wide and total height 3.7 to the top of the roof slope, was not lawful within the meaning of Sections 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\n\r\nThe volume of the proposed extension together with the existing extension to the front of the house, together, exceeds the maximum 50 cubic metre allowance for terraced houses and therefore, not fall within the provisions of Class A, Part 1, Schedule 2 of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development Order) 1995.\r\n"
